{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And the explanation of <b>ולא תענה ברעך עד שוא</b> (“You shall not answer against your fellow a vain witness”) is to prohibit testifying against another even about something of no consequence, for which he would incur no liability at all in court — for example, if he were to testify: \"So-and-so said to give this person a maneh,\" and he did not acquire it from him — for <b>שוא</b> is a worthless thing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:36.224506037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}